---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";
import { TRUST_PROFILES } from "../../config/trust";

const title = "HOA Fees and Mortgage Payment (How to model them)";
const description =
  "HOA dues are part of your housing payment. Learn how to model HOA fees, special assessments, and cash flow impact. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-04-05";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/guides/hoa-fees-and-mortgage-payment"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  robots="noindex, follow"
  authorProfile={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
  reviewProfiles={[TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview, TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview]}
>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">HOA fees</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>HOA fees and your mortgage payment</h1>
    <p>
      HOA dues are not part of your loan balance, but they do affect your monthly housing payment and DTI. This guide shows how
      to include them in your estimates and plan for special assessments.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">Affordability checklist</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <ReviewedByCard
    writtenBy={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
    reviewedBy={TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview}
    secondaryReview={TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview}
    reviewScope="HOA dues treatment inside housing-payment and DTI estimates, special-assessment and reserve-risk framing, and routing between mortgage payment, DTI, and affordability workflows."
    reviewedOn="2026-04-05"
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Use this guide when HOA dues are the missing part of the housing-payment estimate</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Use this page when the mortgage looks affordable until HOA dues or special assessments are layered into the monthly housing cost.</li>
      <li>If you need the full payment formula first, move to <a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">how mortgage payments are calculated</a>.</li>
      <li>If your next question is lender qualification, move next to <a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-dti-housing-payment">mortgage payment in DTI calculations</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Mortgage payment inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan amount, note rate, and term.</li>
      <li>Taxes, insurance, HOA, and PMI assumptions.</li>
      <li>Escrow rules or reserves used by the lender.</li>
      <li>Time horizon if comparing scenarios.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How HOA affects payment</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>HOA dues are added to the housing payment for DTI calculations.</li>
      <li>They do not reduce principal, so they do not affect amortization.</li>
      <li>Fees can change yearly and may include special assessments.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What to confirm</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Monthly dues amount and how often they can change.</li>
      <li>What the HOA covers (insurance, maintenance, utilities).</li>
      <li>Any pending special assessments or reserve shortfalls.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Modeling steps</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Add the HOA monthly dues to your housing payment input.</li>
      <li>Use the total housing payment in DTI comparisons.</li>
      <li>Stress test with a higher HOA amount if increases are likely.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Documents to review</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>HOA budget, reserves, and recent financials.</li>
      <li>Master insurance policy coverage limits.</li>
      <li>Special assessment history and planned projects.</li>
      <li>Rules for dues increases or reassessments.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Why HOA is easy to miss</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      HOA dues do not show up in the loan balance or amortization schedule, so buyers often forget to include them when comparing homes.
      But for cash flow and DTI, they behave like a recurring housing cost and can materially change the affordability picture.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Leaving HOA dues out of the mortgage payment estimate.</li>
      <li>Ignoring special assessments that can raise monthly costs.</li>
      <li>Assuming HOA includes insurance when it does not.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>HOA increase history and any planned hikes.</li>
      <li>Reserve funding level and pending assessments.</li>
      <li>Items covered by HOA vs your own budget.</li>
      <li>Insurance coverage gaps between HOA and personal policy.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">How mortgage payments are calculated</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/mortgage-payment-dti-housing-payment">Mortgage payment in DTI calculations</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/what-is-piti">What is PITI?</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/principal-and-interest-vs-escrow">Principal and interest vs escrow</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Do lenders include HOA in DTI?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Yes, HOA dues are typically included in the housing payment used for DTI.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Can HOA dues change after closing?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Yes. HOAs can raise dues or levy assessments, so keep a buffer for changes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/consumer-tools/mortgages/ready-to-buy-a-home/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Ready to buy a home?
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/owning-a-home/explore/home-loan-toolkit/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Your home loan toolkit
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Run the mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">Check DTI</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/mortgage-payment-affordability-checklist">Affordability checklist</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-04-05</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>



